hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6601","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Yahya al-Bahrani, he said: They mentioned wine with Ibn Abbas, and he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to drink water from him. Shu’bah said: From the night of Monday, so he would drink it on the day of Monday and Tuesday until afternoon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6602","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Abi told us, he said: Warqa’ told us, on the authority of Abi Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya Abi Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “It was served to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the evening, and when morning came, he would drink his day and night until the qibla and the next.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6603","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar: “He was rejected in He would drink waterskins of raisins in the morning, and he would drink them at night, and he would throw them away in the evening, and he would drink them in the morning. He would wash the waterskins, but would not put anything in them. Durdiya, and nothing.” Nafi’ said: We used to drink it like honey."
"6604","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, he said: Ibn Umar used to have raisins thrown out for him. in the evening, and he drinks it in the morning, and it is presented to him in the morning, and he drinks it in the evening.”"
"6605","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Dhar bin Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed Ibn Abd al-Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, said: I asked Ubayy Ibn Ka’b about wine. He said: “Drink water, drink honey, and drink The market, and drink the milk with which you were satisfied. So I went back to him, and he said: Do you want wine?"
"6606","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Aamir bin Abdullah, he said: I read Omar bin Al-Khattab’s letter to Abu Musa: “As for what follows, a camel came to me from the Levant, carrying a thick drink black like camel’s paint, and I I asked them how much they cook it, and they told me that they cook it in two-thirds, two-thirds of which is gone, so please order that They drink it.” Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Lahiq bin Humaid, that Omar wrote to Ammar bin Yasser: As for next. . . , like that"
"6607","Suwayd told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aslam, he said: We came with Omar The tax collector, then he was brought with a robe like the head of the Lord, but he was wading through the waders, and he said: “Indeed, in this drink is what it has reached.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6608","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Maymun bin Mahran, on the authority of Umm Al-Darda’, she said: “ “I used to cook it for Abu al-Darda’ until two-thirds of it was gone and one-third remained.”"
"6609","Kathir bin Ubaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Anas told me, “He was milked for the Messenger of God.” May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A domesticated sheep was in Anas’s house, and its milk turned gray with water from the well. It was given to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. The cup, and he drank from it, until when he took the cup out of it, and on his left was Abu Bakr, and on his right was a Bedouin, Omar said, and he feared that He gives to the Bedouin: Give Abu Bakr with you, O Messenger of God. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave to the Bedouin on his right, and the Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The right hand, then the right hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6610","Ali bin Muslim told us, he said: Yusuf bin Yaqoub told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Anas, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited us in... We turned around and milked a domesticated animal for him, and to the right of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a man from the desert people, and behind the man was Omar. And on the left of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was Abu Bakr. He drank, and Omar said: Give Abu Bakr, so he gave the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He handed over the Bedouin cup and said: “The right hand, then the right hand.”"
"6611","Ubayd Allah bin Faddala told us, he said: I am Muhammad bin Yusuf, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abd God bin Masoud said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not sent down a disease but He has sent down a cure for it, so you should use cow’s milk.” “It shoots from every tree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6612","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Yazid Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not created a disease, but He has created a cure for it, and you should use cow’s milk, for it It shoots from every tree.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6613","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, he said: Hajjaj told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Lot, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Masoud, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “God has not sent down a disease but that He has sent down a cure for it. He mentioned cow's milk, so he ordered it and said: It is a cure for every disease."
"6614","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “ The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade the milk of Galala. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: “The one that eats the offal.”"
"6615","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Rabah, on the authority of Abu Qatada, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The one who guides the people will be the last of them.”"
"6616","Qutaibah bin Sa’id informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Sa’d, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “came With a drink, he drank from it, and on his right was a boy, and on his left were the old men, and he said to the boy: “Permit me to give these things.” So the boy said: O Messenger of God, I would not prefer anyone with my share of you, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took it in his hand.”"
"6617","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Hamza, he said: Zayd bin Waqid told me, he said: Khaled bin Abdullah bin Hussein, he said: Abu Hurairah told me that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter. Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter, and whoever drinks from vessels of gold and silver in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter. The Hereafter, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The clothing of the people of Paradise, the drink of the people of Paradise, and the utensils of the people of Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6618","Humayd bin Masada told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Abdullah bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abu Laila, that Hudhayfah mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not drink from vessels of gold or silver, and do not wear silk. And the brocade, for they are for them in this world, and they are for you in the Hereafter.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6619","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, I think he is on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade us from silver, gold, and from wearing silk and brocade, and said: “For them in this world, and for you in the Hereafter.”"
"6620","Shuaib bin Yusuf told me, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: He said: “The one who drinks from a silver vessel only pours it into His belly is the fire of hell.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6621","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: I am Ismail, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah The Most Gracious, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “He who drinks from a silver vessel only stirs up fire in his belly.” Hell,” on the authority of Amr bin Ali, on the authority of Asim bin Hilal, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ismail bin Masoud, on the authority of Khaled bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He agreed with him, and Ismail bin Umayyah disagreed with him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6622","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb told me, he said: Mahrez told us, I mean Ibn Al-Wadah, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Umm Salamah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The one who drinks from a silver vessel, He only causes the fire of Hell to rage in his belly.” Muhammad ibn Ishaq disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiyya bint Abi Ubaid al-Thaqafi, a woman. Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6623","Amr bin Hisham told me, he said: Muhammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiya, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold or silver will only draw the fire of Hell into his stomach.” Saad bin Ibrahim disagreed with him. He narrated it on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar’s wife, on the authority of Aisha. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6624","Muhammad bin Ismail bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: I am Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’, On the authority of the wife of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one who drinks from a silver vessel is only squirted in His belly is fire.” Sufyan bin Saeed stopped him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6625","Abdah bin Abdullah told us, he said: I am Abu Dawud, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Saad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Safiya, she said Aisha: “Whoever drinks from a silver vessel will only generate fire in his stomach.” Hisham ibn al-Ghaz disagreed. He narrated it on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar."
"6626","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Sadaqah, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Whoever drinks from vessels of gold or silver will only bring the fire of Hell into his stomach.” Burd ibn Sinan followed him."
"6627","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Burd narrating, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Omar, He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever drinks from a vessel of gold, or a vessel of silver, will only cause fire in his belly.” Abdul Aziz bin Abi Rawwad disagreed with him, he narrated it, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, his saying, and he did not mention gold and silver, The correct view of all of this is the hadith of Ayyub, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6628","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: I am Ali and he is Ibn Mushar, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Abu Humayd came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with milk in a cup, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Did you not leaven it? Even if you offered it to him.” \"come back\""
"6629","Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Abu Salama told me, that Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “If he wanted to sleep while he was in a state of junubah, he would perform his ablution for prayer, and if he wanted to eat, Or he drinks, washes his hands, and eats and drinks.”"
"6630","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told me, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade blowing into a vessel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6631","Qutaibah told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, on the authority of his father, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you drinks, he should not breathe into the vessel.”"
"6632","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Azra bin Thabit told us, he said: Thumamah told me, he said: Anas told me, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to breathe into the vessel three times.” It was narrated by Waki’, but he did not mention: in the vessel."
"6633","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Azra bin Thabit Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas, On the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “when he drank, he took three breaths.”"
"6634","Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan told me, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Atiya, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Thumama, on the authority of Anas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he drank, he would breathe two or three times, and Anas used to breathe three times.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: Qatada made a mistake in this hadith, but the correct one is the hadith of Ezra, and God knows best."
"6635","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told me, on the authority of Abu Issam, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you drinks, let him exhale three times, for he will feel better and better.”"
"6636","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abu Issam, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to breathe in When the vessel drinks, and he says: This is a matter, and he narrates it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6637","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and if he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats.” with his left hand, and drinks with his left hand.”"
"6638","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, And he said: “When one of you eats, let him eat with his right hand, and if he drinks, let him drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left hand. And he drinks with his left hand.”"
"6639","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Al-Jawab told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Omar bin Muhammad, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade “that a man should eat with his left hand, or drink with his left hand.” Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6640","Ubaid Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told me, he said: Asim, who is Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Ubaid. Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar said: I heard Salim saying: Abdullah bin Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “They do not eat “One of you should use his left hand, but do not drink with it, for Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6641","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’n told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Suhail, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God A guest, may God bless him and grant him peace, entertained him, and he was an unbeliever, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered a sheep to be milked for him, and he drank its milk. Then another time, so he drank it, and another time, so he drank it, until Hallab drank seven sheep, then the next morning, he converted to Islam, so a messenger gave him orders God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came upon a sheep, and it was milked, and he drank its milk. Then he ordered another, but he did not keep it safe, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “A Muslim drinks in one intestine, and a disbeliever drinks in seven intestines.”"
"6642","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala informed us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Sa`id bin Abi Ayyub informed me, on the authority of Abu Aqeel al-Qurashi, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubali, on the authority of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that whenever he ate or drank, he would say: Praise be to God who fed, watered, and justified it, and made a way out for it.”"
"6643","Ahmad bin Yusuf told us, he said: Abu Al-Mughirah told us, he said: Al-Sari bin Na’am Al-Jablani told us, he said: Aamir bin Jashib told me, on the authority of Khalid bin Maadan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, said: When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was full of food, he would say: “Praise be to God, thanks a lot. good and blessed, neither sufficient nor indispensable.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6644","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told me, on the authority of Aamir bin Jushayb, on the authority of Khalid Ibn Maadan, on the authority of Abu Umamah Al-Bahili, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when the food was over, saying: O God, praise be to You, praise be to You.” “Plenty, good and blessed, not sufficient, not forfeited, not to be dispensed with.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6645","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Khaled bin Ma’dan, on the authority of Abu Umamah, He said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would raise his table, he would say: Praise be to God abundantly, good, blessed, not sufficient, nor farewell. And there is no one who can do without Him, our Lord.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6646","Yunus bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: I am Ibn Wahb, he said: Sa`id told me, on the authority of Bakr bin Amr, on the authority of Ibn Hubayra, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Jubair, from one who served the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, for eight years, that he heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “When the The master is given food: In the name of God. When he finishes his food, he says: O God, you have fed, you have given water, you have enriched, you have provided for, you have guided, and you have collected. So praise be to You for what You have given.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6647","Abu Ubaidah told us, he said: I am Abu Usama, on the authority of Zakaria bin Abi Zaida, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Burdah, on the authority of Anas bin Malik He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, God is satisfied with the servant, whether he eats the food or drinks the drink. And he praises Him for it.”"
"6648","Kathir ibn Ubaid told me, on the authority of Baqiya, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ziyad, he said: Abdullah ibn Busr told me, he said: My father and I were sitting When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to see a mule of his, and my father said: Will you not come down, O Messenger of God, and we will feed you something, and you will pray? With the blessing, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came down and ate, then said: “O God, have mercy on them, forgive them, and bless them in Provide for them (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6649","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he broke his fast with a family, he would say: The fasting people broke their fast with you, and the righteous ate your food.” And the angels descended upon you.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir did not hear it from Anas. Suwayd bin Nasr told us, he said: I am Abdullah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: I narrated on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger Whenever he broke his fast, he, may God bless him and grant him peace, was with the family. . . The chain of the hadith"
"6650","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: Al-Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu al-Ala’ ibn al-Shakhir, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, that He told him, “There was a bowl with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he made the people eat from it. Whenever a people were satisfied and they got up, he sat down.” In their place were other people. He said: Likewise, until the first prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6651","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: I am Waki’, he said: Azra bin Thabit told us, on the authority of Thumama bin Abdullah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas Ibn Malik said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when perfume was brought, he would not reject it.”"
"6652","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you spends the night with a cloud in his hand, and something befalls him, he has no one to blame but himself.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6653","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever spends the night with a cloud in his hand and something befalls him, let no one blame anyone but him.” \"himself\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6654","Zakaria bin Yahya told me, he said: Yusuf bin Wadh told me, he said: Omar bin Ali told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever spends the night with a cloud in his hand has no one to blame but himself.” Abu Abdul Rahman told us: The three hadiths are all wrong, and the correct one is: Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, mursal."
"6655","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told me, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Hamid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: “Did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, feel bad when he built With Zainab, he satiated the Muslims with bread and meat, then he went out to the mothers of the believers, greeted them, prayed for them, and they greeted him. They prayed for him, and he did that on the morning of its construction.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6656","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn 'Abd Allah narrated to us, saying: Abu Ma'mar narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, saying: Qatn Abu al-Haytham narrated to us, saying: Abu Yazid al-Madani narrated to us, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: \"The first instance of qasamah (compurgation) took place in the Jahiliyyah. A man from Banu Hashim hired a man from Quraysh of another clan. He set out with him among his camels. A man from Banu Hashim passed by him whose rope of his leather bag had broken. He said: 'Help me with a rope with which I may tie the rope of my leather bag, so that the camels do not bolt.' So he gave him a rope, and he tied the rope of his leather bag with it. When they halted, the camels were hobbled except for one camel. The one who had hired him said: 'What is the matter with this camel that it was not hobbled among the camels?' He said: 'It has no rope.' He said: 'Where is its rope?' He said: 'A man from Banu Hashim passed by me whose rope of his leather bag had broken, and he called out to me for help. He said: \"Help me with a rope with which I may tie the rope of my leather bag, so that the camels do not bolt.\" So I gave him its rope.' He struck him with a staff in which his fate was sealed. A man from the people of Yemen passed by him. He said: 'Will you attend the pilgrimage season?' He said: 'I do not attend it, though perhaps I may attend it.' He said: 'Will you deliver a message from me once in a lifetime?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'When you attend the pilgrimage season, then call out: \"O family of Quraysh!\" When they answer you, call out: \"O family of Banu Hashim!\" When they answer you, ask for Abu Talib and inform him that so-and-so killed me on account of a rope.'\" He said: \"The hired man died. When the one who had hired him arrived, Abu Talib came to him and said: 'What happened to our companion?' He said: 'He fell ill, and I took good care of him. Then he died, and I took charge of his burial.' He said: 'He was deserving of that from you.'\" He said: \"He remained for a while. Then the Yemeni man to whom he had entrusted the delivery of the message arrived at the pilgrimage season. He said: 'O family of Quraysh!' They said: 'This is Quraysh.' He said: 'O family of Banu Hashim!' They said: 'This is Banu Hashim.' He said: 'Where is Abu Talib?' They said: 'This is Abu Talib.' He said: 'So-and-so instructed me to deliver a message to you: that so-and-so killed him on account of a rope.' Abu Talib came to him and said: 'Choose one of three things from us: if you wish, you may pay a hundred camels, for you killed our companion by mistake; or if you wish, fifty of your people may swear oaths that you did not kill him; and if you refuse, we shall kill you in retaliation for him.' He went to his people and mentioned that to them. They said: 'We will swear oaths.' A woman from Banu Hashim came to him who was married to a man among them and had borne him a child. She said: 'O Abu Talib, I would like you to exempt my son, this man, from being one of the fifty, and not require his oath.' So he did that. Then a man from among them came to him and said: 'O Abu Talib, you wanted fifty men to swear oaths in place of a hundred camels, so that each man would receive two camels. Here are two camels, so accept them from me, and do not require an oath where oaths are sworn.' So he accepted them. Then forty-eight men came and swore oaths.\" Ibn 'Abbas said: \"By Him in whose hand is my soul, the year had not passed before, of the forty-eight, not a single eye remained without being struck.\""
"6657","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh and Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Ibn Wahb informed us, saying: Yunus informed me, about Ibn Shihab said: Abu Salamah and Suleiman bin Yassar told me about a man from the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Ansar. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “approved the division as it was in pre-Islamic times,” and the wording is for Ahmad."
"6658","Muhammad bin Hashim Al-Baalbaki told us, he said: Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abi Salamah, and Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of some of the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The division took place during pre-Islamic times, so he approved it.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as it was in pre-Islamic times, and he judged it among some of the Ansar regarding a murdered man whom they claimed against the Jews of Khaybar. \". Abu Abdul Rahman said: Muammar disagreed with them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6659","Muhammad bin Rafi’ al-Naysaburi told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, He said: The punishment was in pre-Islamic times, “Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, approved it in the case of the Ansari who was found killed in the Jews’ pit.” The Ansar said: The Jews killed our friend. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6660","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh informed us, saying: Ibn Hub informed us, saying: Malik ibn Anas informed me, on the authority of Abu Laila ibn Abd. Allah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari, that Sahl ibn Abi Hathamah informed him, that Abdullah ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah went out to He was informed of an attack that had befallen them, so he came to Muhayyisah, and was informed that Abdullah bin Sahl had been killed, and thrown into a poor person or a spring, so he came Jews, and he said: By God, you killed him. They said: By God, we did not kill him. Then he approached until he came, so he mentioned that to them, then he came back. He and Huwayysah, who is his older brother, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl. So Huwayysah, who was the one who was in Khaybar, went to speak. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Allahu Akbar, Allahu Akbar, and Huwayysah spoke, then Muhaiysah spoke, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And peace be upon him: Either they will destroy your friend, or they will announce war. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote about that, so they wrote: “Indeed, by God.” We did not kill him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Huwayysa, Muhaiyya, and Abd al-Rahman: “You swear, and you deserve the blood of Your friend? They said: No. He said: So the Jews will swear to you. They said: They are not Muslims. He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid homage to him from his side, so he sent They came to them with a hundred she-camels until they entered their house.” Sahl said: “A red she-camel galloped past me.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6661","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn al-Qasim told us, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Abu Laila bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Sahl, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Abi Hathamah, that he and prominent men of his people informed him that Abdullah Ibn Sahl and Muhayyisah, They went out, meaning to Khaybar, because of a struggle that befell them, and Muhaiyyasah came and reported that Abdullah bin Sahl had been killed, and thrown into a poor man, or A spring, so the Jews came and said: You killed him. They said: By God, we did not kill him. He continued until he came to his people, so he mentioned to them, then He and his brother Huwaysa, who was older than him, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl came, so Huwaysa went to speak, and it was he who was In Khaybar, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to Muhaiysah: “Grow up, speak out, he wants to be old.” So Huwayysah spoke, then Muhaiysah spoke. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Either they will destroy your friend, or they will announce the call to war. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wrote to them. And peace be upon him, so they wrote: We, by God, did not kill him. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Huwayysa and Muhayysa, And Abdul Rahman: Do you swear, and are you worthy of the blood of your companion? They said: No. He said: So do the Jews swear to you? They said: They are not Muslims. So he ransomed him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came from him, so he sent to them with a hundred she-camels until they entered their house. Sahl said: You have ridden me. Among them is a red camel (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6662","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, and he said: I thought that he said: On the authority of Rafi’ bin Khadij, that they said: Abdullah bin Sahl bin Zayd and Muhayyisah bin Masoud went out until While they were in Khaybar, they dispersed somewhere there, then in Muhaiyyas, he found Abdullah bin Sahl dead, so he buried him, then he came back. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he, Huwaysa bin Masoud, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, who was the youngest of the people, so he went. Abdul Rahman spoke before his two companions, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “He has grown old, he has grown old, so he remained silent, and his two companions spoke.” Then he spoke to them, and they mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, the killing of Abdullah bin Sahl, and he said to them: Will you swear by fifty? An oath, and do you deserve your companion or your killer? They said: How can we swear, when we do not bear witness? He said: Will the Jews acquit you with fifty oaths? How can you accept the oaths of an unbelieving people? When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw that, he gave him his reason."
"6663","Ahmad bin Abdah Al-Basri told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah and Rafi’ bin Khadij told him that Muhaiyya bin Masoud and Abdullah bin Sahl came to Khaybar in There was a need for them, so they dispersed among the palm trees, and Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, so his brother Abdul Rahman bin Sahl, Huwaysa, and Muhaiysa came. His cousin, to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdul Rahman spoke about the matter of his brother, who was younger than them, so the Messenger of God said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The older one, let the older one begin.” So they talked about the matter of their companion, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said, and mentioned A word that means: “Should fifty of you swear?” They said: O Messenger of God, this is something we have not witnessed. How should we swear? ! He said: Will the Jews absolve you of the faith of fifty of them? They said: O Messenger of God, these are infidel people! So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him before him. Sahl said: So I entered a shelter of theirs, and a she-camel of those camels galloped past me."
"6664","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Bishr told us, and he is Ibn al-Mufaddal, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah and Muhaiysah bin Masoud bin Zaid, they came to Khaybar, which was peaceful on that day, and they separated for their needs. Then Muhayyisa came to Abdullah bin Sahl, and he was drenched in the blood of a dead man. He buried him, then he came to Medina, and Abd al-Rahman bin set off. Sahl, Huwaysa, and Muhaisah to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdul Rahman went to speak, and he was the youngest of the people in age. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He became very arrogant, so he remained silent, and they spoke, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: You will swear. With fifty oaths from you, and do you deserve the blood of your companion, or your killer? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we swear when we do not bear witness and have not seen? He said: Will the Jews acquit you with fifty? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we take the oath of an infidel people? \"from him\""
"6665","Ismail bin Masoud Al-Basri told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, On the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, he said: Abdullah bin Sahl and Muhaiyya bin Masoud bin Zaid set off for Khaybar, which was on that day. They reached peace, and they separated to discuss their needs. Muhayyisa came to Abdullah bin Sahl while his blood was dripping, so he buried him, then he came to Medina. Then Abd al-Rahman ibn Sahl, Muhayysah, and Huwayysah ibn Masoud went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abd went The Most Gracious was speaking, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “He became very arrogant, and he was the youngest of the people. So he remained silent, so they spoke, and he said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: You will swear by fifty of you, and you will be worthy of your killer or your companion. They said: O Messenger of God, how? We swore, but we did not bear witness, and we did not see it. He said: Will the Jews disavow you with fifty? They said: O Messenger of God, how can we take the oath of an infidel people? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made sense of it from him.”"
"6666","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Wahhab told us, he said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed, saying: Bashir bin Yasar told me, about Sahl bin Abi Hathamah said that Abdullah bin Sahl Al-Ansari and Muhaiyya bin Masoud went to Khaybar and separated for their needs. Then Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, so Muhayysah came, and Abdul Rahman, the brother of the one who was killed, and Huwayysah bin Masoud, until they came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. So Abdul Rahman went to speak, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “The arrogance is the arrogance, so Muhayyisah spoke. And Huwaisa. They mentioned the case of Abdullah bin Sahl, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You swear fifty, so you will be entitled to He fought you? They said: How can we swear if we did not bear witness and were not present? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Will the Jews acquit you with fifty? O Messenger of God, how can we accept the oath of an infidel people? He said: So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to him. Bashir bin Yassar said: Sahl said to me. Ibn Abi Hathamah: I performed one of those obligations in a place of ours. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6667","Muhammad bin Mansour Al-Makki told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahl Ibn Abi Hathamah said: Abdullah Ibn Sahl was found dead, so his brother came, and his two uncles were Huwaisa and Muhaiysa, who were Abdullah’s uncles. Ibn Sahl went to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abdul Rahman went to speak, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pride.” Arrogance, they said: O Messenger of God, we found Abdullah bin Sahl killed in the heart of Khaybar, meaning, in the heart of Khaybar. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Who do you accuse? They said: We accuse the Jews. He said: So you swear by fifty oaths that the Jews killed him? They said: How do we swear by what they did not? See? He said: So the Jews will exonerate you with fifty because they did not kill him? They said: How can we be satisfied with their oaths, when they were polytheists? May God bless him and grant him peace.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Malik bin Anas sent him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6668","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, and I heard, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bashir Ibn Yasar, that he informed him that Abdullah Ibn Sahl Al-Ansari and Muhaiyya Ibn Masoud went to Khaybar, and they dispersed in Their needs were met, so Abdullah bin Sahl was killed, so Muhayysah came, so he and his brother Huwayysah and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl came to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so Abdul Rahman went to speak; Because of his place in front of his brother, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Grow up, grow up.” Huwayysah and Muhaiysah spoke, and they mentioned the matter of Abd. Allah bin Sahl, then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to them: Will you swear fifty oaths, and will you be worthy of the blood of your friend or your killer? \". Malik said: Yahya said: Bashir claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid homage to him. Abu Abdul Rahman said: Saeed bin Ubaid Al-Tai disagreed with them."
"6669","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Sa’id bin Ubaid al-Tai told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, and he claimed that A man from the Ansar, called Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, told him that a group of his people went to Khaybar and dispersed there. They found one of them dead, so they said to those who found him with him: You killed our friend. They said: We did not kill him, nor did we know who killed him. So they went to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they said: O Prophet of God, we set off for Khaybar, and we found one of us killed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: “Arrogance is arrogance.” So he said to them: “Will you bring proof of who was killed?” They said: “We have no proof.” He said: “Then they will swear to you.” They said: “No.” We are satisfied with the faith of the Jews. The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, hated to have his blood shed in vain, so he paid him a hundred camels as charity.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: We do not know that anyone followed Saeed bin Ubaid Al-Tai on the wording of this hadith, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar and Saeed bin Ubaid is trustworthy, and his hadith is more likely to be correct in our view, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6670","Muhammad bin Muammar Al-Basri told us, he said: Ruh bin Ubadah told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Al-Akhnas told us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather, said that Ibn Muhayyasa the Younger was killed at the gates of Khaybar, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Arise. Two witnesses to the one who killed him. I will hand him over to you in its entirety. He said: O Messenger of God, and from where did he get hit? Two witnesses, but he was killed on the Their doors? He said: So he swore fifty oaths? He said: O Messenger of God, and how can I swear on what I do not know? He said: “Should we make fifty of them swear to God?” He said: “O Messenger of God, how can we make them swear to God when they are Jews?” So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore He bestowed his blood money upon them, and helped them with half of it.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: We do not know that anyone followed Amr bin Shuaib on this narration, nor did Saeed bin Ubaid follow his narration, on the authority of Bashir bin Yassar, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6671","Bishr bin Khalid Al-Askari Al-Basri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I heard Abd Allah bin Murrah, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is not permissible to shed the blood of a Muslim except in one of three ways: \"One life for another, the married man who commits adultery, and the one who abandons his religion.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6672","Muhammad bin Al-Ala Abu Kurayb Al-Kufi, and Ahmad bin Harb, told us the wording, saying: Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: A man was killed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the killer was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him, so he gave him to the guardian of the murdered person, and the killer said: O Messenger of God, no, by God, I did not want to kill him, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He greeted the guardian of the murdered person: “But if he were truthful, then you killed him, you entered the Fire.” So he let him go, saying: He was wrapped in a blanket. So he went out dragging his saddlebag, so he was named Dhu Al-Nasaa, the pronunciation is for Ahmad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6673","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Ulayya, the judge of Damascus, informed me, saying: Ishaq al-Azraq told us about the deprivation of the Bedouins, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wael Al-Hadrami, on the authority of his father, said: The murderer who was killed was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the guardian of the murdered person brought him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “Do you pardon?” He said: No. He said: Do you take the blood money? He said: No. He said: Murder? He said: Yes. He said: Go. When he went, he said: If you pardon him, he will bear your sin and the sin of his companion. So they pardoned him. So he sent him, saying: I saw him dragging his saddlebag. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6674","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Awf bin Abi Jamila, he said: Hamza Abu Omar Al-A’idhi told me He said: Alqamah bin Wa’il told us, on the authority of Wa’il, who said: I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the killer was brought, led by a guardian. The person who was killed was in Nasa'ah, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to the guardian of the murdered person: \"Do you pardon?\" He said: No, he said: Do you take the blood money? He said: No, he said: So you kill him? He said: Yes. He said: Take him away. When he took him away, he summoned him and said to him: Will you pardon him? He said: No. He said: Do you take the blood money? He said: No. He said: So you kill him? He said: Yes. He said: Go. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: As for Indeed, if you pardon him, he will bear his sin and the sin of his companion.” So he pardoned him and left him, saying: I saw him dragging his head. Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Jami’ bin Matar al-Hubati told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il, on the authority of his father, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. . . By the same token. Yahya said: He is better than him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6675","Amr bin Mansour told us, he said: Hafs bin Omar, who is Al-Hudhi, told us, he said: Jami’ bin Matar told us, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wa’il. On the authority of his father, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man with a sting on his neck came and said: “O Messenger of God, This man and my brother were in a pit digging, so he raised his beak and hit his companion in the head with it, killing him. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pardon me. Then he refused, and got up and said: O Prophet of God, this man and my brother were in a pit digging it, so he raised the beak and hit his head with it. His companion, and he killed him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Pardon him, but he refused, then he got up and said: O Messenger of God, this man and my brother were in A hole they dig, so he raised his beak and I saw him. He said: He struck his companion in the head and killed him. He said: Pardon him, but he refused. He said: Go. You killed him, you were like him, so he took him out until he passed, so we called him: Do you not hear what the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, says? Then he returned and said: If I killed him, would I be like him? He said: Yes, pardon him. So he went out, dragging his body, until it was hidden from us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6676","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Hatem bin Abi Saghira told us, on the authority of Simak, he mentioned that Alqamah bin Wael told him, on the authority of his father, that he was sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came to him, leading another with his horse. He said: O Messenger of God, this killed my brother. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: “You killed him?” He said: O Messenger of God, if you had not He confessed. I established proof against him. He said: Yes, I killed him. He said: How did you kill him? He said: He and I were cutting firewood from a tree, so he insulted me. So he made me angry, so I hit his horn with the ax, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Do you have any money to pay for yourself? He said: O Messenger of God, I have nothing but my axe and my cloak. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: Do you think your people will buy you? He said: Me It is easier for my people than that. So he threw the spear at the man and said: Your friend is better than you. When he left, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he kills him, then he will be like him. Then they caught up with the man and said: Woe to you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If he kills him, then he will be like him. So he returned to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, it was narrated that you said: If he kills him, then he is like him, and is Did you take him except by your command? He said: You do not want him to bear your sin or the sin of your companion? He said: Yes. He said: So that is the case. Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Muadh told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Abu Yunus, and he is Hatim bin Abi, told us Small, on the authority of Simak bin Harb, that Alqamah bin Wael told him that his father said: I was sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when a man came to him Leading another. . . Towards him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6677","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told us, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Alqamah bin Wael, that his father Wael told them that a man who had killed another man was brought to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he brought him to the guardian of the murdered person to kill him. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to those sitting with him: “The murderer and the killed will be in Hell.” He said: A man followed him and informed him. When he informed him, he left him. He said: I saw him dragging his shoulder when he let him go, so I mentioned that to Habib, and he said: Sa’id bin Ash’wa told me, he said: And he mentioned it to me. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded the man to pardon (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6678","Issa bin Yunus Al-Fakhouri told us, he said: Damra told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shawdhab, on the authority of Thabit Al-Bunani, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that a man brought the murderer of his guardian to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Pardon him,” but he refused. He said: Take the blood money, but he refused. He said: Go and kill him, for you are like him. So he went and followed the man, and he was told: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Kill him, for you are like him.” So he cleared his way, and the man passed by me while he was dragging his horse. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6679","Al-Hasan bin Ishaq Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Khalid bin Khidash told us, he said: Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Bashir bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father, that a man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a man, and said: This man was killed. My brother, he said: “Go and kill him as he killed your brother.” So the man said to him: Fear God, and pardon me, for it is greater for your reward and better for you. And for your brother on the Day of Resurrection. He said: So he abandoned him. He said: Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed. He asked him, and he told him what he told him. He said: Did you free him? Was it not better than what will be done to you on the Day of Resurrection? He will say: O Lord, ask this man why he killed me? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6680","Al-Qasim bin Zakaria bin Dinar told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Ali, who is Ibn Salih, told us on the authority of Simak, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “There were Qurayzah and al-Nadir, and al-Nadir was more honorable than Qurayzah, and whenever he killed a man from Qurayzah A man from al-Nadir, he was killed for it, and when a man from al-Nadir killed a man from Qurayzah, he sacrificed a hundred wasqs of dates. When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was sent Peace and blessings of God be upon him. A man from al-Nadir killed a man from Qurayza. They said: Give him to us and we will kill him. They said: Between us and you is the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So they came to him, and then it was revealed: And if you judge, judge between them with justice, and justice: a life for a life, then it was revealed: Is the most correct of pre-Islamic times? They want (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6681","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, he said: Dawud ibn Husayn told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: The verses in the table Concerning which God said: Then judge between them or turn away from them to those who are just. Rather, it was revealed regarding blood money between Banu al-Nadir and Banu Qurayza. This is because those who killed an-Nadir were honored, and they paid the full blood money, and the Banu Qurayza used to pay half the blood money, so they disputed that matter. to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and God Almighty revealed that about them, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, carried them to the truth in That, so He made the blood money equal.”"
"6682","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told me, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qays bin Abbad, he said: Al-Ashtar and I went to Ali and said: Did the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entrust you with something that he did not entrust to people in general? He said: No, except for what is in this book of mine. So he took out a book from the scabbard of his sword, and lo and behold, in it was: “The believers’ blood will be repaid, and they will be defeated. Whoever is besides them, and the lowest of them seeks to fulfill their obligation. Is not a believer killed for an unbeliever, nor a covenant person during his covenant, whoever commits an act, so he should himself, or harbors an infidel, upon him is the curse of God, the angels, and all mankind.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6683","Abu Bakr bin Ali Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Al-Qawariri told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahid told us, he said: Omar told us Ibn Amir, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ali, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The believers will be rewarded for their blood.” “And they are a hand on everyone else, and the one who is closest to them seeks their protection. A believer will not be killed for an unbeliever, nor will a covenant person be killed during his covenant.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6684","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills him, We will kill him, and whoever makes him single, We will make him single.”"
"6685","Nasr bin Ali told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, it was said: It is from the Sahih that is not heard, except for the hadith of the Aqeeqah, for it was said to Al-Hasan: From whom did you hear the hadith about the Aqeeqah? He said: From Samura, and not all scholars authenticate this narration. He said: I said to Al-Hasan: From whom did you hear the hadith about the Aqeeqah? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6686","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.”"
"6687","Yusuf bin Saeed bin Muslim Al-Masisi told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Dinar told me that He heard Tawus speaking, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar, that he sought the judgment of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in that matter, so Hamal ibn Malik stood up, He said: “I was between my two wives’ rooms, and one of them hit the other with a flat, killing her and her fetus, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the death sentence.” And he was safe in her fetus by surprise, and that she might be killed therein.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6688","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdah bin Sulaiman al-Kufi told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas: A Jew killed a slave girl over her clothes, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, drove him away with them.”"
"6689","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak Al-Makhrami told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Aban bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, “that a Jew took some cloth from a slave girl, then smashed her head between two stones, and they overtook her and he fell asleep.” So they started following the people after her. Is it this? She said: Yes. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave an order, and he complied. His head is between two stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6690","Ali bin Hajar informed us, he said: Yazid bin Harun informed us, on the authority of Hammam bin Yahya, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Anas, he said: “It came out A slave girl was wearing scarves, so a Jew took her, crushed her head, and took the jewelry she was wearing. She was brought to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Who killed you, so-and-so? She said with her head: No. He said: So-and-so. He said: Until he named the Jew She said with her head: Yes, so he was taken and confessed, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to do so, and his head was crushed with two stones."
"6691","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah Al-Naysaburi told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim, who is Ibn Tahman, told me, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rufai’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, Mother of the Believers, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: “No It is permissible to kill a Muslim except in one of three cases: a married adulterer, in which case he will be stoned; a man who intentionally kills a Muslim, in which case he should be killed; and a man who is expelled from Islam, so he fights against God and His Messenger, and is killed, or crucified, or banished from the land.”"
"6692","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Tarif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard Abu Juhayfa, saying: We asked Ali, so we said: Do you have anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, other than the Qur’an? He said: No, by the One who split the grain and caused the breath, unless God gives a servant understanding of His Book, or what is in this document. We said: And what In the newspaper? He said: “It includes reason, the redemption of a prisoner, and that a Muslim should not be killed by an infidel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6693","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj bin Minhal told us, he said: Hammam told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan, he said: he said Ali: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not entrust me with anything other than the people, except a scroll in the skin of my sword. They did not remove it until he took out the scroll. So, it contains: “The blood of the believers will be rewarded, the lowest of them will pursue their duty, and they will have a hand on everyone else. A believer will not be killed by an unbeliever. And there is no one who has a covenant in his covenant.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6694","Ahmad bin Hafs bin Abdullah told us, he said: My father told me, he said: Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Al-Hajjaj, On the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan al-Araj, on the authority of al-Ashtar, that he said to Ali: The people have interceded for what they hear, so if the Messenger Has God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a covenant with you, so tell us about it? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not entrust me with a covenant that he did not entrust to the people, except that in the skin of my sword was a scroll, and behold, in it: “The blood of the believers will be rewarded, and the one who is closest to them will seek their protection. A believer will not be killed by an infidel, nor will a covenant be kept in his covenant,” Mukhtasar"
"6695","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Uyaynah, he said: My father told me, he said: Abu Bakra said: The Messenger said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever kills a person who has made a covenant in a state other than his due form, God will forbid Paradise for him.”"
"6696","Al-Hussein bin Harith Abu Ammar told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath bin Thurmalah, On the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Whoever kills a soul who has made a covenant without solving it, God will forbid him Paradise unless \"He smells her scent\""
"6697","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymarah, on the authority of a man from the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a man from the people of He will not smell the scent of Paradise, and indeed its scent will be felt from a distance of seventy years.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6698","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim Duhaim told us, he said: Marwan, who is Ibn Muawiyah, told us, he said: Al-Hasan, who is Ibn Amr, told us, On the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Junada bin Abi Umayyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a person “From the people of the people of the people of the people of Dhimma, he has not smelled the fragrance of Paradise, and its fragrance is felt from a distance of forty years.”"
"6699","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Nadra, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn said, “A boy of poor people cut off the ear of a boy of rich people. They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not give them anything.” \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6700","Ishaq told us, he said: Abu Khaled Suleiman bin Hayyan told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He ruled for retaliation for old age, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Book of God is retaliation.”"
"6701","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills his servant, We will kill him, and whoever kills his servant, We will kill him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6702","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar told us, saying: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Samurah, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever castrates his servant, We will castrate him, and whoever castrates his servant, We will castrate him.” The wording by Ibn Bashar (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6703","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Thabit told us, on the authority of Anas, that a sister Al-Rabi’, Umm Haritha, wounded a person, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Retaliation.” Retaliation. Umm al-Rabi’ said: O Messenger of God, should I retaliate against so-and-so? No, by God, he will never be retaliated against. So the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said. Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Glory be to God, O Umm al-Rabi’, retaliation is God’s book. She said: No, and God will never retaliate against her. So she continued until they accepted the blood money. He said: “Indeed, among the servants of God is he who, if he swore an oath to God, would fulfill it.”"
"6704","Humaid bin Masada Al-Basri and Ismail bin Masoud told us, saying: Bishr told us, on the authority of Humaid, he said: Anas mentioned that His paternal aunt broke the jawbone of a slave girl, so the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled for retaliation. Then her brother Anas ibn al-Nadr said: Will the jawbone be broken? So-and-so? No, by the One who sent you with the truth, so-and-so’s neck will not be broken. He said: And before that, they had asked her family for forgiveness and compensation, so when her brother swore, He is the uncle of Anas, and he was the martyr on the Day of Uhud. The people were satisfied with the pardon. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, among the servants of God are those who swear On God, to be righteous.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6705","Muhammad ibn Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, he said: Al-Rabi’ broke a running girdle, So they asked them for pardon, but they refused, so they were offered compensation, but they refused, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he ordered retaliation. He said: Anas ibn al-Nadr: O Messenger of God, will the tawny of al-Rabi’ be broken? ! By the One who sent you with the truth, do not break it. He said: “O Anas, the book of God is retaliation.” The people were satisfied and pardoned, and he said: Among the servants of God are those who I swear on God that I will fulfill it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6706","Ahmad bin Uthman, known as Al-Jawza Basri, told us: Quraysh bin Anas informed us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man bit another man’s hand, so he tore off his hand, and his jawbones fell off, or he said: his jawbones, so the Messenger of God attacked him. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “What do you command me to do? You command me to command him to put his hand in your mouth, so that you bite it.” Like a stallion gnawing, if you wish, so give him your hand until he gnaws it, then take it away if you wish.”"
"6707","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man bit another on the arm, so he pulled it, and his folds were torn out, so that matter was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him. He said hello, then he invalidated it and said: “You wanted to bite your brother’s flesh like a stallion bites?”"
"6708","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, and Muhammad bin Bashar told us He said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: I heard Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, he said: Ali fought a man, so he bit One of them was his friend, so he took his hand from his mouth and removed his folds, so they disputed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “One of you will bite.” His brother bites like a stallion! He has no blood money for him.” The wording is by Ibn Bashar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6709","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd al-Marwazi informed us, saying: Abdullah informed us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that Ya’la said about the one who was bitten and his beard became thin: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You do not have to pay blood money.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6710","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Abu Hisham told us, he said: Aban told us, he said: Qatada told us, he said: Zurara bin Awfa told us, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that a man bit the arm of a man, and he tore out his collar, so he went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, mentioned that to him, and he said: “You wanted to bite your brother’s arm like a stallion bites it?! So he annulled it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6711","Malik bin Al-Khalil Al-Basri told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ali bin Minya, that he killed a man, and one of them bit his friend, so he tore his hand from his mouth, so he extracted his tooth, and that matter was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him. He greeted him and said: “One of you bites his brother as he bites a firstborn!” So he invalidated it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6712","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Aqeel Al-Basri told us, he said: My grandfather told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ya`la bin Munya, that a man from Banu Tamim fought a man, and he bit his hand, so he snatched it, and he threw his buttocks, so they disputed. To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “One of you bites his brother as he bites a firstborn!! So he invalidated it,” that is, he invalidated it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6713","Imran bin Bakkar al-Humsi told us, he said: Ahmad bin Khalid told us, he said: Muhammad, who is Ibn Ishaq, told us on the authority of Ata Bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Safwan bin Abdullah, on the authority of his two uncles, Salama bin Umayyah, and Ya`la bin Umayyah, who said: We went out with the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the Battle of Tabuk, and with us was a companion of ours. He fought a Muslim man, and the man bit his arm and pulled it from his mouth. So he put down his folds, and the man came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, seeking reason, and said: “One of you will go to his brother and bite him hard.” The stallion, then he comes asking for the mind! She has no mind, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, invalidated it! (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6714","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of His father, “A man bit another man’s hand and his collarbone was torn out, so he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and destroyed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6715","Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Ala told us again, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of Ya’la, And Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan ibn Ya’la, on the authority of Ya’la, that he hired a worker, and he fought a man, and he bit his hand, and it was torn off. I bent it, so he took it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “He lets her bite it like a stallion bites?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6716","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of his father, He said: “I went on a campaign with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk, so I hired an employee, and my employee fought with one man, and he bit the other, and I fell.” I bent it, so he came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and mentioned that to him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, destroyed it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6717","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Ibn Ulayya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ataa told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, on the authority of Ya’la bin Umayyah, said: I invaded the army of hardship with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and my best deeds were in Myself, and I had a worker, and he fought a man, and one of them bit his friend’s finger, and he tore out his finger, and he lowered his fold, and it fell, So he went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he lowered his beard and said: “Should he leave his hand in your mouth so that you can bite it?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6718","Suwayd bin Nasr told us in his hadith, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Ya’la On the authority of his father, for example: Concerning the one who was bitten and his beard became weak, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “There is no blood money for you.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6719","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Badil bin Maysarah, On the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la bin Munya, that an employee of Ya’la bin Muniya bit his last arm, so he tore it out of it, and it was lifted. That was up to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his second had fallen off, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, invalidated it and said: “Leave it in Why do you gnaw it like a stallion gnaws? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6720","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told me, he said: Abu Al-Jawab told us, and his name is Ahwas bin Jawab, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Safwan bin Ya’la, that his father invaded He was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the Battle of Tabuk. He hired a worker, and he fought a man. The man bit his arm, and when it hurt him, he We saw it, and he warned his second, and this was reported to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “One of you bites his brother just as he bites The stallion? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6721","Wahb bin Bayan Al-Masry told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdullah, On the authority of Ubaidah ibn Musafa’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id al-Khudri, he said: “While the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was dividing something, a man approached. So he leaned on him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stabbed him with a cripple he had with him, so the man came out, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Come, so be patient,” and he said: “Rather, I have pardoned.”"
"6722","Ahmad bin Saeed Al-Maruzi told me, he said: Wahb bin Jarir told us, he said: my father told us, he said: I heard Yahya, speaking, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Musafa’, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was dividing Something happened when a man fell on him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stabbed him with a cripple he had with him. The man shouted, and the Messenger of God said to him: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Come and lie down.” The man said: “Rather, I forgive you, O Messenger of God.”"
"6723","Ahmad ibn Sulayman al-Rahwi informed us, saying: Ubayd Allah informed us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, that he heard Sa`id ibn Jubayr, He says: Ibn Abbas told me that a man had an affair with a father he had in pre-Islamic times, and Abbas slapped him. Then they came to his people and said: To strike him as he had struck him, so they put on weapons, and that reached the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, so he ascended the pulpit and said: “O people! Do you know who the people of the earth are most honorable to God? They said: You. He said: Indeed, Al-Abbas is from me, and I am from him. Do not curse our dead, lest you harm them. He revived us.” Then the people came and said: O Messenger of God, we seek refuge in God from your anger. Ask forgiveness for us. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6724","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maymun Al-Raqqi told me, he said: Al-Qanabi told me, he said: Muhammad bin Hilal told me, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. He said: We used to sit with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the mosque, and when he stood up, we stood up. He stood up one day, so we stood up with him, until when He reached the middle of the mosque, and a Bedouin overtook him, so he pulled his robe behind him, and his robe was rough, so his neck turned red, and he said: Oh Muhammad, carry these two camels for me, for you will not carry from your own wealth, nor from your father’s wealth. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No, And I ask forgiveness from God. I will not carry you until you bind me with what you have tied to my neck. The Bedouin said: No, by God, I will not restrain you. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He greeted that person three times, each time saying: No, by God, I will not restrict you. So when we heard what the Bedouin said, we quickly approached him, and he turned to us. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I have determined that whoever hears my words will not leave his place until he is given permission. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said And he greeted a man from among the people: “O so-and-so, carry barley for him on a camel, and on a camel of dates.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Go away.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6725","Mu'mal bin Hisham Basri told us, he said: Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abu Masoud Saeed bin Iyas Al-Jariri told us, On the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Firas, that Omar said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “narrating to himself.”"
"6726","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ al-Naysaburi informed us, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “sent Abu Jahm bin Hudhayfah as a charity, and a man urged him on his charity. Abu Jahm beat him, so they came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: The fuel, O Messenger of God, and he said: “For you such-and-such.” They agreed, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: I He addresses the people and informs them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed him and said: These people came to me wanting food. So I offered them such-and-such, and they agreed. They said: No. The immigrants understood them, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered them to desist, so they desisted. Then he called them and said: Are you satisfied? They said: Yes, he said: I will address the people, and inform them of your satisfaction. They said: Yes, so he addressed the people, then he said: Are you satisfied? They said: Yes. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6727","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hisham bin Zayd, on the authority of Anas, that a Jew saw He killed her with a stone, then she was brought to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked at her and said: “Did so-and-so kill you?” Shu’bah pointed. With his head he said it, \"No.\" He said: \"Did so-and-so kill you?\" Shu'bah pointed with his head and told it, \"No.\" Then he said: \"Did so-and-so kill you?\" A lump in his head says it, yes, “So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, called for him and killed him between two stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6728","Muhammad bin Al-Ala informed us, saying: Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent A expedition to a people from Khath'am, but they persisted in prostrating, and were killed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled that half the reason should be made, and he said: “I He is innocent of every Muslim who associates with a polytheist. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Will their fire not be seen? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6729","Al-Harith bin Miskin read about it, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “He was among the Children of Israel Retaliation, but there was no blood money among them, so God Almighty revealed: Retaliation for the murdered is prescribed for you: the free for the free and the slave for the slave until His saying: Whoever is pardoned from his brother in any way, then he should follow through with kindness and return it to him with kindness. Forgiveness means that he accepts the blood money intentionally. So, following with a good deed, he says: He follows this one with a good deed, and performs it with a good deed, and he performs this one with a good deed, that is an alleviation of the burden. Your Lord has not decreed for those before you, but it was retaliation, not blood money."
"6730","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Abdullah, who is Ibn Bakr bin Abdullah, told us. Al-Muzani, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Maimunah, on the authority of Anas, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought about retaliation, and he ordered that it be pardoned.”"
"6731","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Bahz bin Asad, and Affan bin Muslim told us, they said: they told us Abdullah bin Bakr Al-Muzani said: Ata’ bin Abi Maimunah told us, and I do not know of him except on the authority of Anas bin Malik. He said: “The Messenger of God was not given May God’s prayers and peace be upon him regarding anything that involves retaliation, unless he commands pardon in it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6732","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ash’ath al-Dimashqi informed us, saying: Abu Mushar narrated to us, saying: Ismail, who is Ibn Abd, narrated to us. By God, Al-Awza’i told him, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Abu Salamah told me, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Whoever has someone killed has the choice of two options: either he will be led away, or he will be ransomed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6733","Al-Abbas bin Al-Walid bin Mazid told us, he said: my father told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, he said: Yahya told me, he said: he told me Abu Salamah, he said: Abu Hurairah told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever has someone killed for him, is the one with the best of two options.” Either he will be led, or he will be redeemed.” Ahmad bin Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Ibn Aidh told us, he said: Yahya told us, he is Ibn Hamza, he said: he told me Al-Awza’i, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, he said: Abu Salamah told me, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Who A man was killed by him (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6734","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Hisn told me, he said: Abu Salamah told me, and Al-Hussein told us Ibn Harith, he said: Al-Walid told me, he said: Al-Awza’i told me, he said: Hisn told me, that he heard Abu Salamah, speaking on the authority of Aisha, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “And those who fight must be detained first, then first, even if it is a woman.”"
"6735","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Sa`id bin Sulayman told us, he said: Sulayman bin Kathir told us, he said: Amr bin Sulayman told us. A dinar, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever is killed among a blind person or a dead man, you will be among them.” With a stone, or with a whip, or with a stick, then his mind is a mistaken mind, and whoever is killed intentionally, his hand must be cut off, and whoever comes between him, must The curse of God, the angels, and all of mankind, no retaliation or justice will be accepted from it.”"
"6736","Muhammad bin Muammar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Kathir told us, he said: Sulayman bin Kathir told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawoos On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he narrates it. He said: “Whoever is killed by a blind eye, or by throwing a stone, or with a whip, or with a stick, has the mind of error.” And whoever kills intentionally, then he is a retaliation, and whoever comes between him and him, the curse of God, the angels, and all of humanity is upon him. God will not accept it. There is no justice in it, and there is no justice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6737","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Ayoub al-Sakhtiyani, on the authority of al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one killed by mistake, almost intentionally, by a whip or a stick, One hundred camels, forty of them with their young in their bellies.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6738","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim told me, he said: Yunus, who is the son of Muhammad al-Muddib, told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, On the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabia, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “gave a speech on the day of the conquest.” sender (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6739","Yahya bin Habib bin Arabi told me, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Uqba bin Aws, On the authority of Abdullah, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The one killed by mistake, almost intentionally, was not killed with a whip or a stick.” A hundred camels, forty of which had their young in their bellies.”"
"6740","Muhammad bin Kamil Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Uqba bin Aws, on the authority of A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he said: “The one who was killed by mistake Striking with a whip, a stick, and a stone, a hundred camels, of which forty camels were equal to Basil its year, all of them camels.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6741","Muhammad bin Bashar informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Adi, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Uqba bin Aws, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Indeed, the one who was killed by mistake, the one who was killed by the whip and the stick, among them are a hundred camels, gagged, forty of them in their bellies.” \"Her children\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6742","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Ibn Aws, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered Mecca on the day of the conquest, he said: Indeed, for every person killed by mistake intentionally, or semi-intentionally, by the whip or the stick, there are one hundred camels in it, of which forty are in their bellies. \"Her children\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6743","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Ya’qub bin Aws, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him that when the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to Mecca in the year of the conquest, he said: “ Indeed, the one killed by mistake, almost intentionally, the one killed by the whip and the stick, there are a hundred camels, of which forty, meaning, have their young in their bellies. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6744","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Sahl bin Yusuf told us, he said: Humaid told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, that the Messenger of God prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The mistake is semi-intentional, meaning the stick and the whip, including a hundred camels, of which forty were in their bellies.” \"Her children\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6745","Muhammad bin Mansour told us, he said: Sufyan told us, he said: Ibn Jud’an told us, he heard it from Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Ibn Omar, He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up on the day of the conquest of Mecca on the steps of the Kaaba, thanked God and praised Him, and said: “Praise be to God.” To God, Who is true to His promise, and grants victory to His servant, and defeats the parties alone. Indeed, the one who is killed intentionally and accidentally, with the whip and the stick, is like... Al-Amd, in which there are a hundred camels with thick hair, including forty calves with their young in their bellies.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6746","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ informed us, saying: Yazid informed us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Aws. A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Mecca in the year of the conquest. He said: “Unless “The one killed by deliberate mistake, the one killed by the whip and the stick, of which forty had their children in their wombs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6747","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, he said: Yazid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Rashid told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever kills a dead person, his ransom is one hundred camels.” Thirty are the daughters of Makhad, thirty are the daughters of Labun, thirty are Haqqah, and ten are males of the sons of Labun. He said: We found the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And he gave the value of four hundred dinars to the people of the villages, or an equal amount of paper, and he valued it to the people of the camels, when they boiled, he raised it in Its value, and if it depreciated, its value decreased as it happened over time, then it reached its value during the era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Between four hundred dinars and eight hundred dinars, or an equivalent amount of paper. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled: Whoever The owner of the cows is entitled to two hundred cows, and whoever has the right to sheep, two thousand sheep, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. He said: The mind is an inheritance according to their obligations, so whatever is left over is for the clan, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed that the mind should be given to the woman. Her descendants are whoever they are, and they do not inherit anything from it, except what is left over from her heirs, and if she is killed, then her inheritance is among her heirs, and they are They kill her killer.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: This is an objectionable hadith, and Sulaiman bin Musa is not strong in hadith, nor is Muhammad bin Rashid. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6748","Ali bin Saeed bin Masruq told us, saying: Yahya bin Zakaria bin Abi Zaida told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, On the authority of Khashf bin Malik, he said: I heard Ibn Masoud saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided the blood money for the sinner was twenty bint Makhad. “Twenty males from Bani Makhad, twenty from Bint Labun, twenty from Jadah, and twenty from Haqqah.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Al-Hajjaj ibn Artaat is weak and cannot be used as evidence."
"6749","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, on the authority of Muadh ibn Hani, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated to me, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, and he informed us Abu Dawud, he said: Muadh bin Hani told us, he said: Muhammad bin Muslim told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “A man killed another man during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made his blood money twelve thousand. He mentioned his saying: “And they did not resent it except that God and His Messenger enriched them of His bounty by taking blood money from them,” and the wording is by Abu Dawud. Muhammad bin Maimun told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, we heard him once, saying: on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “paid for twelve thousand, meaning the blood money.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Muhammad ibn Muslim is not strong, and the correct one is mursal, and Ibn Maimun is not strong either. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6750","Issa bin Yunus al-Ramli told us, he said: Damra bin Rabi’ah al-Ramli told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ayyash, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A woman’s mind is like a man’s mind, even It amounts to one-third of her blood money.” Abu Abdul Rahman said: Ismail bin Ayyash is weak and makes many mistakes."
"6751","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, and he mentioned a word that means: about Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The mind of the people of the people of Dhimma is half the mind of the Muslims.” They are the Jews and Christians.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6752","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh informed us, he said: Ibn Hub informed us, he said: Usama bin Zayd informed me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The mind of an infidel is half the mind of a disbeliever.” \"the believer\""
"6753","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Waki’ told us, Ali bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided in the offices. The blood money for a freed man must be killed according to what he paid.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6754","Muhammad bin Ubayd Allah bin Yazid told us, he said: Othman told us, he said: Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “decided in the offices that the blood money of a freed man should be paid in proportion to what he freed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6755","Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ali narrated to us, on the authority of al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a decree. In the offices, the amount of what he paid from the office shall be paid as blood money for the freed man, and whatever remains is blood money.” \"slave\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6756","Muhammad ibn Isa al-Dimashqi told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, and on the authority of Ayyub On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The one who is appointed will be freed from him in proportion to what he has delivered, and he will be held accountable for it.” The limit is in proportion to the amount of it he is freed from, and he inherits in proportion to the amount of it he is freed from.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6757","Al-Qasim bin Zakariya told us, he said: Saeed bin Amr told us, he said: Hammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that a conscript was killed during the reign of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he ordered “That the blood money of a free man should be paid as blood money, and what he paid as the blood money of a slave.”"
"6758","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub and Ibrahim bin Yunus told us, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Yusuf bin Suhayb told us, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, on the authority of his father, said that a woman omitted another woman’s miscarriage, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave her five children One hundred sheep, and on that day he forbade the omission.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Nu`aym sent him"
"6759","Ahmad bin Yahya told me, he said: Abu Naim told us, he said: Yusuf Ibn Suhayb told us, he said: Abdullah bin Buraidah told me, That a woman kidnapped another woman, and the one who had been kidnapped miscarried, so that matter was reported to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. “So he made five hundred pieces of her child’s offspring.” Of sheep, and on that day he forbade killing them.” Abu Abd al-Rahman told us: This is an illusion, and he must have wanted a hundred sheep. The prohibition against cutting was narrated on the authority of Abd Allah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Mughaffal (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6760","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: He told us in a whisper, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Abdullah bin He was foolish, because he saw a man cheating, so he said: “Do not cheat, for the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to forbid cheating, or he disliked it.” \"The kidnapping.\" He doubted in a whisper (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6761","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Tawus, that Omar consulted people about the fetus, and he said that Ibn Malik: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed the fetus by surprise.” Tawoos said: The horse is a fringe"
"6762","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ibn Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He decreed The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was in the fetus of a woman from Banu Lahyan, who fell dead with the forelock of a male or female slave. Then the woman who He ruled that her inheritance should go to her children and her husband, and that the mind is upon her. \"Her nerves\""
"6763","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abd al-Rahman and Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that he said: Two women from Hudhayl fought, and one of them shot the other. With a stone, and he mentioned a word that means: I killed her and what was in her stomach. So they disputed to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided. May God bless him and grant him peace, the blood money for her fetus is a male slave, or a female child, and he decreed the blood money for a woman on her female relative, and inherited from her to her son. And those who were with them, then Hamal bin Malik bin Al-Nabigha Al-Hudhali said: O Messenger of God, how can I be fined if one does not drink, eat, speak, or initiate? ! Something like that would appear, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is one of the brothers of soothsayers, because of the prostration that he prostrated.”"
"6764","Ahmad bin Amr bin Al-Sarh told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that two women from Hudhayl, in the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, threw Her fetus, “and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made a ruling regarding it, with the help of a male slave or a female child.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"6765","Al-Harith bin Miskin, reading from him, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “deceased the fetus, to be killed in its mother’s womb, with the prey of a male slave, or a female girl.” Then the one who judged him said: How? Will the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, be fined? \"Soothsayers\""
